  body: |
    # Benefit-specific scope of reciprocal agreements

    ## Authored interpretation

    The guidance distinguishes agreements with EEA and non-EEA countries and says the country lists specify the benefits covered. It expressly warns that provision for Incapacity Benefit does not itself establish ESA(C) coverage.

    ## Scope and boundaries

    DMG 070310–070312; country and benefit coverage must be checked in the applicable agreement and version. The association with EC coordination is not equivalence or permission to transfer a rule.

    ## Inspected source passages

    - [DMG 070310, PDF page 57](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69ce3908bed91051df63a90e/dmg0701.pdf#page=57)
    - [DMG 070312, PDF page 57](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69ce3908bed91051df63a90e/dmg0701.pdf#page=57)

